# Install

Build Rocci from this repository, then preview a component. There is no
crates.io package and no install script. GitHub Release archives exist as an
experimental prerelease channel; do not start there unless you already know
you want those binaries.

This manual is for programmers who are new to Rocci. It does not teach
programming from zero. You should be able to read typed code, use a terminal
and Git, and edit a text file.

Commands below run from the repository root. They use
`cargo run -p rocci-cli`. That is the documented spelling until an installed
`rocci` distribution exists.

`@fixture` declarations are **experimental** syntax for previewing components
(`rocci view` / `rocci browse`) and possibly for tests. They do not change
generated component functions.

## Toolchain

| Tool | Role | As tested |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rust and Cargo | Build the Rocci workspace | GitHub Actions `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`, edition 2024 crates |
| Roc nightly | Compile generated and authored Roc | `nightly-2026-08-10` (`7df8509`), pinned in `docker/install-roc.sh` |
| Native webview | Preview window | macOS WebKit, Linux WebKitGTK 4.1, Windows system webview |

A mismatched Roc nightly can reject syntax that is valid for this repository.

Optional primers: [Roc](/docs/appendix/roc-for-rocci/),
[Datastar architecture and runtime](/docs/appendix/web-foundations/). Full Roc
lives at [roc-lang.org](https://www.roc-lang.org/).

## Install Rust and Roc

Install a Rust toolchain that compiles this workspace (edition 2024).
[rustup](https://rustup.rs/) is the usual path.

Install Roc. This repository is tested against **Roc nightly-2026-08-10**
(`7df8509`). See the [Roc install docs](https://www.roc-lang.org/install) and
match that nightly when a listed nightly is available. Confirm:

```sh
roc version
rustc --version
```

## Clone and build

```sh
git clone https://github.com/koliyo/rocci.git
cd rocci
cargo build -p rocci-cli
```

## Desktop applications and preview

:tabs.begin[group: "install-os", kind: "platform"]
    :tab[id: "mac", label: "macOS"] {{
        Tao and Wry use the system WebKit view. No extra webview packages.
        Ad-hoc `.app` bundling is available later with `rocci bundle`.
        Verified in CI (`macos-latest`).
    }}
    :tab[id: "linux", label: "Linux"] {{
        Install the WebKitGTK development packages Wry needs. On Debian and
        Ubuntu this matches CI (`ubuntu-latest`):

        ```sh
        sudo apt-get update
        sudo apt-get install -y \
          libgtk-3-dev libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev \
          libappindicator3-dev librsvg2-dev patchelf
        ```

        Other distributions use their WebKitGTK 4.1 development packages.
        Headless checks can pass `--no-window`.
    }}
    :tab[id: "windows", label: "Windows"] {{
        Wry uses the operating-system webview. Windows packaging is not
        implemented. Development `rocci run` / `rocci view` use the same local
        HTTP server as other platforms. This path is not in CI.
    }}
:tabs.end

## Preview a component

Confirm the CLI and lower the styling example:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- --help
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

The build command prints generated Roc to stdout. You should see a `hello`
function and `Html.element` calls.

Then open the component (window or browser):

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

The command prints a local URL. With `--no-window`, the default port is `8000`.

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `roc` not found | Roc missing from `PATH` | Install the pinned nightly and retry `roc version` |
| WebKit / webview link errors on Linux | Missing GTK/WebKitGTK dev packages | Install the packages above or use `--no-window` |
| Template compilation failed | Checkout is incomplete | Run from the clone root; do not copy a single `.rocci` file out of tree |

### Experimental GitHub archives

CI publishes `rocci-{version}-{target}.tar.gz` archives on GitHub Releases
(macOS aarch64 and Linux x86_64). Treat them as **experimental**. They are not
the first-run path in this manual.

Next: [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/five-minutes/).
